{
 "source": "geneva",
 "book": "JOS",
 "chapter": 11,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.1",
   "range": "JOS.11.1",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6a67fe57",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.1#p1-6a67fe57",
     "text": "The more God's power appears, the more the wicked rage against it.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "sent to Jobab king of Madon"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.2",
   "range": "JOS.11.2",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e54598a5",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.2#p1-e54598a5",
     "text": "Which the evangelists call the lake of Gennesaret, or Tiberias.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "Chinneroth"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.3",
   "range": "JOS.11.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "82c724bd",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.3#p1-82c724bd",
     "text": "Which was mount Sion, as in De 4:48.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "Hermon in the land of Mizpeh",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "De 4:48",
       "ref": "DEU.4.48"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.6",
   "range": "JOS.11.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "4e7e1096",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.6#p1-4e7e1096",
     "text": "That neither they should serve to the use of war, nor the Israelites should put their trust in them.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "hough their horses"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.8",
   "range": "JOS.11.8",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "3a184c92",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.8#p1-3a184c92",
     "text": "Which signifies hot waters, or according to some, brine pits.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "Misrephothmaim"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.11",
   "range": "JOS.11.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "4a886ae7",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.11#p1-4a886ae7",
     "text": "Both men, women and children.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "souls that were therein with the"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.13",
   "range": "JOS.11.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "8e56de2f",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.13#p1-8e56de2f",
     "text": "Which were strong by situation and not hurt by war.",
     "label": "g",
     "anchor": "strength"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.14",
   "range": "JOS.11.14",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ed8f5cb5",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.14#p1-ed8f5cb5",
     "text": "All mankind.",
     "label": "h",
     "anchor": "man they smote with the edge"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.16",
   "range": "JOS.11.16",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1dd0cfc0",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.16#p1-1dd0cfc0",
     "text": "That is, Samaria.",
     "label": "i",
     "anchor": "mountain of Israel"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.17",
   "range": "JOS.11.17",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "73318fca",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.17#p1-73318fca",
     "text": "So called, because it was bare and without trees.",
     "label": "k",
     "anchor": "Halak"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.20",
   "range": "JOS.11.20",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1aebdbc6",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.20#p1-1aebdbc6",
     "text": "That is, to give them over to themselves: and therefore they could not but rebel against God and seek their own destruction.",
     "label": "l",
     "anchor": "harden their hearts"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.11.22",
   "range": "JOS.11.22",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "81321c94",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.11.22#p1-81321c94",
     "text": "Out of which came Goliath, 1Sa 17:4.",
     "label": "m",
     "anchor": "in Gath",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Sa 17:4",
       "ref": "1SA.17.4"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
